WEBVTT

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.450
Thinking that we could actually win must have jinxed us.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.870
Droves and droves of Jovian fleets came swarming toward us.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.710
If only we could have saved the survivors in exchange for our lives.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.490
Nadesico Broadcast

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:53.710
Three!
Nadesico Broadcast

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:54.300
Three!

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.050
Two!

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:55.800
One!

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.200
Ka-Boom!

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.790
Wow!

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.780
Hey! It's "Get to Know the Nadesico!"

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.510
Currently broadcasting inside vessel

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.910
Hey, everyone, come closer!

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.380
It's time to talk about the secrets of the Nadesico!
Currently broadcasting inside vessel

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:09.350
Come closer.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:15.230
The "Song" That You Will One Day Sing

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.700
Everyone, do you know what makes the Nadesico go?

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.630
I'd like to know, oneesan!

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:21.930
So cute!

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:22.830
Nee, nee. Tell me.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:23.160
So cute!

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.210
Well, Nadesico relies on the Phase Transition Engine.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.290
That's not it!

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:25.600
Well, Nadesico relies on the Phase Transition Engine.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.450
Ruri-ruri's so cute!

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:27.520
Well, Nadesico relies on the Phase Transition Engine.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:28.920
Nee nee, oneechan!

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.270
I used to be on programs like this.
What ist it Usagi-chan?

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:31.440
I used to be on programs like this.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.710
Well, that's a good question.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.130
Let's talk about the Nadesico's Phase Transition Engine.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.890
Here, come over here.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:39.280
Wait a second! I still have lines left!

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.690
I see, so that's it!

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.810
Can you tell me which water tank has the most potential energy?

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.710
Well, no, I can't tell.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:51.400
I'm only a rabbit after all!

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.200
Well, it's this one, the one that's the most elevated.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.100
This water tank represents the high degree of potential energy

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.210
that was contained in the vacuum of space immediately following...

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.240
Wait, Hoshino Ruri!

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:00.800
that was contained in the vacuum of space immediately following...

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.040
The good little children of the Nadesico are watching this!

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.550
Please follow the script!

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.870
Come on, turn to the camera with a smile on your face, oneesan!

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:08.560
Baka...

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.310
Don't let it bother you! Just relax, Ruri-chan.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.800
Now we'll take it from where we left off!

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.300
No, you won't!

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.710
What is the meaning of this ridiculous stunt, Fressange?

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.130
After a concentrated barrage of gravity blasts from the enemy,

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.290
our engine output is down to below half strength.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:28.880
The Distortion Field is weak,

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.920
and we cannot reach escape velocity to leave Mars atmosphere.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.820
I hardly think turning this into a parody is appropriate.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:37.320
You're the one who took away the place I called home.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.910
Please don't blame Inez-sensei!

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.020
It's all for my sake!

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:47.490
Inez-sensei is nice enough to defend the actions that I took as Captain to the crew...

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.490
I... I...

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:50.820
Baka?!

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:54.200
It's not a matter of forgiving after a situation like that.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.250
And I don't know how to put this, but...

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.680
I guess I'm a different from most people when it comes to here.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.600
Oh, don't get me wrong. I mean my heart.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.210
I can see that you're strange.

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:10.260
You see, I don't have any memories from before I was eight.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.420
Even the age of eight is a rough estimate.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.990
I was found abandoned in the desert on Mars.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:20.190
Maybe that's the reason why none of this seems to be real.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:24.990
This might sound rude, but to me,
who's dead and who's alive doesn't mean much.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.600
All right, let's continue!

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:34.250
If you could give me a kiss,

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.620
I can keep going.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.710
It would keep me going a little longer.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.260
That was a close...

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:45.600
No, no, no!

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.680
I'm not interested in her one bit!

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:49.100
Right, Gai?

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:50.320
Right?

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:57.080
Who did it?! Who took my Gai?!

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:00.660
The solid metal Gekiganger 3 limited collector's model!

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:06.950
Oh, Admiral!

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:08.660
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:13.670
That's why the vacuum immediately after the Big Bang

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.750
contained a high degree of potential energy.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.000
You mean high like this?

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:16.890
How is it?

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:17.180
You mean high like this?

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:18.750
This is iced tea, right, Sir?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.610
Fool. This is just an example.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.190
They're rather picky about some regulations. I spiked it just a little. Fool.

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.800
It's believed that all vacuum went through a phase transition

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.840
I don't think regulations like that are limited to the military.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.130
and released a lot of energy while the universe expanded.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:30.640
This is referred to as the Inflation Theory.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.920
This balloon's energy rating is lower than the water tank, right?

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.020
This is our current universe.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:41.800
So what if there was a vacuum that had even less potential energy?

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.360
By phase transitioning the vacuum surrounding the ship into a state

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:45.590
where it can hold less energy, we gain huge amounts of energy!

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:47.430
Am I going to be scolded?

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:48.670
Do you like it?

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:49.240
where it can hold less energy, we gain huge amounts of energy!

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:49.490
This is the principle behind the Phase Transition Engine.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.800
Ah, yes.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:52.480
I'll leave it behind.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:55.010
So, the turning water wheel is the Phase Transition Engine and...
You can have as much of it as you like.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:56.260
Uh, thanks.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.340
With access to such large amounts of energy secure,

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:02.840
we can regulate gravity within the ship

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:05.260
and fire the Gravity Blast Cannon as much as we like.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.690
My Gekiganger!

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.260
Didn't you just shoot that off with your finger?

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.930
Don't let details like that bother you.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.510
Where is the right arm for the Gekigan Punch?

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.860
Put some effort into looking for it!

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:20.360
Hey, Akito, I think I'm all right.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:22.620
I'll work hard to make sure I won't worry you.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:27.280
Who thought of an invention like phase transitioning a vacuum?

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:27.700
Was it you?

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.350
Heavens, no!

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.960
No one invented it.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:32.740
We found it.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.370
Found it? The engine?

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:41.010
Good work, all of you! It was a very, very nice program!

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:42.650
Nice work, Goat-kun.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:43.820
Well, I was drawn in.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:46.810
But why don't we end right about now.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:49.510
Electricity isn't cheap. I'm sure you understand!

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:49.830
The End

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.560
Watch us again!

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:51.630
The End
The End

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.560
Did you understand that, lzumi?

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.440
Darn, you're fast asleep!

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.400
Well, time to get back to work.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.530
Well, thank you!

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.760
You really don't mind?

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:09.950
Oh no, please go ahead.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:13.380
Tenkawa-san's son? So you were at the Utopia Colony?

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.100
Yes.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:18.340
Wow, I'm surprised you were willing to board this ship!

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:19.370
Why?

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:23.580
It's so strange.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:24.800
Why would that be?

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:28.380
Looking at your face makes me feel nostalgic for some reason.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.470
You two are getting far too close!

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:32.880
What is it all of a sudden?!

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.600
Oh, I just remembered. We have some important news.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.850
Akito and Inez-san, please come up to the bridge!

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:40.450
Let's go.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:41.940
You mentioned...

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.230
Yes?

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:43.930
Why?

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.190
Why would I have a problem being onboard this ship?

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:47.940
Any responses?

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:50.560
The friend or foe identification signal has just come back.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.280
It matches our records.

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:56.090
Then there's no doubt that it is...

00:07:56.470 --> 00:08:00.460
But it doesn't make sense. She was lost on Earth.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:01.670
So why...

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:07.850
Why would Crocus be on Mars when it was sucked into a Chulip?

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:09.550
As I explained before,

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:11.890
the Chulip should be thought of less as the Jovian's mothership

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:15.310
and more like a wormhole of some sort or perhaps a gate.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.420
It would make sense that a vessel sucked into a Chulip on Earth

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:20.540
would materialize on Mars, wouldn't it?

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.370
Then the Jovian Lizards emerging from the Chulips on Earth

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.650
are coming from Mars?

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.170
That might not necessarily be the case, you know.

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:35.920
Think about that other ship that was sucked into the same Chulip...

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.340
What was her name?

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.140
The Pansy.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.540
There's no sign of the Pansy nearby.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.580
Think how useful it would be if there are numerous exits.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:46.450
We will launch the Hinagiku.

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:49.510
There is no need for that. We must hurry on to our destination.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:53.430
But there might be survivors on board. Right, Admiral?

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:56.770
We will abide by Nergal's guidelines.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.640
Excuse me. I have something I'd like to ask.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.190
What are you doing, coming here so late?!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.570
Admiral, is it true that you led our forces in the First Battle of Mars?

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.390
Well now, you can listen to war stories later!

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.730
Everyone knows Admiral Fukube was in charge at the battle.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.460
What's wrong with you, Akito?

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.220
Yeah, I know.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.440
The hero who managed to sink enemy Chulips.

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:28.800
But an entire Martian colony was obliterated on that day.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:33.340
All hands abandon ship!

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:41.600
So you're the one!

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:47.270
You did it! You! You!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:52.410
What are you doing? This isn't like you!

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:54.760
Okay, now it's time to be quiet, right?

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.640
Hey, I'm impressed. I like him!

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:00.910
That enthusiasm just means that he'll rush into an early grave.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:04.170
No matter the circumstances, it's unforgivable that a crew member

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.640
physically assaulted the commander of our fleet.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:09.000
Yurika, I mean Captain, please dispense a stiff sentence!

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:10.700
Jun-kun!

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:13.030
But punishment for Akito...

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:14.920
What would be appropriate?

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:18.850
Well, we can get to that later. Please observe this first.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:21.260
Near the north pole, where the Nadesico is currently heading,

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:24.020
a research laboratory is located on the frozen tundra.

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.790
With luck, we may be able to find a spare Phase Transition Engine.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:27.940
Admiral!

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.450
Deploy Aestivalis for reconnaissance.

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:48.330
Oh man, look at this thing crawl.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.250
I just can't make myself like this Heavy Arms Frame.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:54.170
You lucky bastards! You're too lucky!

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:56.380
Ice covered ground.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.060
Ice is a drag.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.170
So, where is this laboratory?

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:08.970
I've been referencing the map, but I can't find it anywhere.

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:10.890
Quiet! Someone's here!

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:15.320
Like I said, don't suddenly turn into a deadly serious lzumi...

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.030
Oh, my gosh!

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:17.660
What is it?!

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:18.810
Where's the enemy, lzumi?!

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.990
I can't see. It's not anywhere we can see.

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:28.960
Sorry, Ryoko! It's coming your way!

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:29.870
Coming?

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:37.450
Damn it, I'm stuck in this Heavy Arms Frame!

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:42.450
Hey, wait a minute.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.600
No way! No way, no way!

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.010
Izumi! Hikaru!

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:48.180
Tenkawa!

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:11.540
Thank you!

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:13.250
So what will it be?

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:16.130
I heard it!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.920
You got it all wrong, idiots!

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.070
I meant we'd have a better formation with another pilot here!

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:22.140
Tenkawa!

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.860
All right! What do you want from me?!

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:27.900
I think I'll have the pudding a la mode!

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:29.410
The genmai tea set, please.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.210
Surrounded by five Chulips on its perimeter.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:33.860
This doesn't look good.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:33.950
Nadesico Strategy Room

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:37.480
But it's the duty of the employees to retake that facility.
Nadesico Strategy Room

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:41.390
Please remember that you are employees of this corporation.

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.200
Are you telling us to just barge on in there?

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:47.870
I'd prefer not to recklessly subject the crew to such danger.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.220
We'll use her.

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:50.500
Her?

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.560
Come on, get it done in three minutes!

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.810
Won't you please reconsider, Admiral?

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:56.770
It's far too dangerous!

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:57.670
I will go!

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:01.120
I do not believe that you know how to pilot a vessel manually.

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.610
And we are merely going to survey the ship at this point.

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:07.160
Okay, I understand that much, but why do I have to go?

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.090
Consider it your punishment.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:13.350
We'll be counting on you, Akito-kun.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:25.910
The Crocus disappeared from Earth two months ago.

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.990
But it looks like it's been buried in the ice here for more than that.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.570
No, buried for a much longer period of time than that.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:36.170
It takes the Nadesico six weeks to reach Mars with her Phase Transition Engine.

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:39.680
Are you saying Chulips can send matter through warped space?

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:43.170
Sounds like something from that TV program, Geki-something.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:44.590
I'm a little uncomfortable with the term warped space.

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:49.790
My reserach shows when enemy vessels emerge from a Chulip,

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:53.620
boson and photo-graviton particles are emitted.

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.660
In other words, an increase in the boson phenomenon.

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:00.650
If Chulips take advantage of the supersymmetry between fermion...

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:18.210
I'm not worthy of such protection. You need not strain yourself.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:19.920
My body just acted on its own.

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:30.120
It appears that the propulsion nozzles are clogged with ice.

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:31.930
Would you mind cleaning it out?

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:32.900
Me?

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:34.850
Fressange, would you mind helping him?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.800
I doubt he would be able to figure it out on his own.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:37.220
Yes.

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.710
The nozzles looks like they're exposed enough for it to work.

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:44.940
What is it?

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:47.620
Get back, Aestivalis! This ship is taking off!

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:52.470
Crocus has taken off.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.840
Well, it looks like it's perfectly operational.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:01.100
The Admiral certainly knows his way around!

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.950
In the shape the Nadesico is in currently,

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:09.390
even the Crocus would probably be able to rupture her hull.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.310
What's come over you, Admiral?!

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:16.220
He is instructing us to enter the Chulip in front of us.

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:17.690
Enter the Chulip?

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:19.780
Why?

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:22.060
Take a look at the shape that the Crocus is in.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:24.990
The Nadesico would not fare any better once inside the Chulip.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:28.180
You're saying he wants to destroy the Nadesico?

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:29.570
For what purpose?

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.450
He wants to cover up his own misdeeds!

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:35.140
He's going to lay the blame on someone else and get away alone!

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:37.370
If that was true, you're the first one he'd kill.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:41.590
Damn jeezer!

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:44.880
They found us?

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:49.050
Port 145 degrees, elevation 80 degrees, enemy fleet approaching.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:51.290
Lesser of two evils, I suppose.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:54.630
We either fight it out against the Crocus or plunge into the Chulip.

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:56.620
I guess we go for the Chulip then.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.520
What are you saying?!

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:01.280
This is nuts! We'll only lose money!

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:05.030
Ruri-chan, pull back and recover the Aestivalis.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:08.020
Minato-san, work out a course to enter the Chulip on the double.

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:10.870
Captain, I can't let you do this!

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:14.330
You're about to break your contract with Nergal.

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:16.770
If we maneuver around, we should be able to sink the Crocus and...

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:21.250
Have you no faith in the Admiral you selected?!

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:25.370
Damn him!

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:25.870
Damn it!

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:27.350
Hey, Tenkawa!

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:28.840
Damn it!

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:32.680
Wait just a second, Yurika! What the hell are you thinking?!

00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:41.940
Yes, you certainly are sharp, Captain.

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:46.820
Entering the Chulip.

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:50.690
Are you sure this is a good idea?

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:53.130
The Crocus is following us.

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:57.700
Turn back, Yurika!

00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:00.550
What the hell are you thinking?! Turn around now!

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:06.710
The crew of the Crocus were all dead! We'll end up just like them!

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:10.810
That's not necessarily true.
We have the Distortion Field.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:13.130
Steady as she goes.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:15.620
The highest priority of the engine is to maintain field stability.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:16.260
Yurika!

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:17.740
The Admiral...

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:21.060
He's giving us the best chance we have to escape Mars.

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:22.140
That's impossible!

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:24.960
That can't be! This isn't making any sense at all!

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:26.220
Tenkawa...

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:29.650
The Crocus has turned about dead in front of the Chulip and halted.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:31.560
Does he intend to fight?!

00:17:35.310 --> 00:17:35.820
Admiral!

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:40.240
If the ship blows itself up where it is now, they would not be able to come after us.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:43.350
Why are you all making this look so noble and honorable?!

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:44.660
Admiral, please don't do this!

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:48.340
The Nadesico, no, I still need you alongside me!

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:52.260
I don't know what to do without your guidance!

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:56.090
I have nothing I can teach you.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:18:01.810
I merely do this to protect those who are dear to me.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.430
What does that mean?!

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:04.970
I cannot tell you what it is.

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:07.610
But I am certain each of you have it within yourselves.

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:10.050
Or I should say, you will find out soon.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:16.280
I was not a good admiral.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.690
I probably was no better a man.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:23.040
Here I am forcing others to abide by my wishes to the bitter end.

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:25.040
But let me just say this.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.660
The Nadesico is your ship.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:32.080
The anger, the hatred, the love, all of what you feel onboard is yours.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:34.380
Words mean nothing. For...

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:36.260
Admiral!

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:44.170
Turn back now!

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:44.990
I can't!

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:46.770
It's as if some invisible force is pulling us in!

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:48.690
The Chulip has disappeared.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:54.710
I have no idea what will follow next.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:57.030
All hands, prepare for shockwaves.

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:05.340
I remember. There was an episode of Gekiganger just like this.

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:09.080
A guy goes down, protecting his friends.

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:11.060
It sounded so cool.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.860
I never thought it would happen to me.

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:18.330
Why do we have to be saved by someone like him?

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:23.580
He was doing it to satisfy himself. He was just pulling a stunt!

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:32.600
Even before you found out about his past, Tenkawa, it seems you're the only person he left a message for.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.400
He was set on dying on Mars from the very beginning.

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:38.820
But he met you and wanted at least...

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:41.740
So, forgive him?

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.070
I should be thankful to him?!

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:45.780
He should have lived!

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:47.710
For the sake of all those who died on Mars,

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.280
he should have lived on with his miserable life!

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:53.810
And that's what we're going to do!

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.420
To have intended on dying from the very beginning...

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:58.800
That's being too irresponsible.

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:02.020
Doing something when you're old to make up for what you did before

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:03.950
is an idiotic idea to start with.

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.510
A fool's a fool no matter how old the person is.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:12.270
But who are we to learn from now?

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:14.400
Who will teach us?

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.240
You look as lovely as always, Erina-kun.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:22.790
Nergal Heavy Industrials - Presicent's room

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:26.840
The Nadesico has left Mars after suffering tremendous losses.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.410
Just as we expected, I suppose.

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:32.450
Guess we move on to project B.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:33.330
Can't be helped.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.750
I will board the Nadesico as well.

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:38.920
Get me the Supreme Commander of the UEAF.

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.650
Yes, it's time to make up.

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:46.950
Hi, everyone!

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:49.820
Did you enjoy this week's episode of "Get to Know the Nadesico"?

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:51.960
Now you've learned all the secrets of the Phase Transition Engine,

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:54.510
the Gravity Blast Cannon, and even about supersymmetry.

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:56.760
Well, next week will be about a formula.

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:59.370
On a space ship that has just enough fuel and food,

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:01.180
the addition of just one stowaway can sometimes make it impossible

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:03.080
for the ship to arrive at its destination.

00:22:03.080 --> 00:22:06.140
Tom Godwin called this the "Cold Equation".

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:08.480
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:10.550
"The Luke Warm Cold Equation"

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:12.470
Let's watch it, everyone, OK?!
